Description: rhi: gl: give a swapchain the eye targets of a window that becomes stereo
 .
 A platform may give a shown window's surface a second view, or take it away,
 by recreating the surface with another number of views: the Wayland platform
 does this while an engine draws the window once per eye. The swapchain built
 the left and right render targets only when it was created or resized, from
 the format the window had then, so a window that became stereo had no right
 buffer to render into until it was resized, and one that stopped kept a right
 target that no longer existed.
 .
 The swapchain now follows the window's format at the start of each frame,
 after making the context current, which is where the platform gives the
 surface the views it now has.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
